==Enemy==
Wicked Tank Cat is basically a nerfed [[Crazed Tank Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Tank Cat]] with the [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] trait. It has a good amount of health, though not nearly as much as Crazed Tank Cat or [[Manic Eraser Cat (Enemy)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and 10 less range than either of them. Its attack power and DPS are very low, but it has a guaranteed chance for a level 1 [[Surge Attack|Surge]] that can reach past its attack. Overall, whereas Crazed Tank Cat destroys tanky cats with ease but falters against a spam of weaker cats, Wicked Tank Cat is the opposite, keeping weak meatshields away, yet lacking the power to do much about tanks that get in close proximity.

==Strategy==
Since it doesn't hurt much even with Surges, tanky cats like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]] or [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]] are highly effective against it.

Even much later on, in [[Infernal Tower]] [[Infernal Tower/Floor 45|Floor 45]], Wicked Tank Cat only does 6,000 damage per hit and ends up behind the [[Oldhorn]] and [[Bakoo]]s in the stage, so rushing it down with [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attackers]] like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] is advised.

